1
00:00:32,741 --> 00:00:34,300
I'm hungry.

2
00:00:59,699 --> 00:01:01,199
If I do this,

3
00:01:02,229 --> 00:01:04,013
no one can touch you?

4
00:01:23,052 --> 00:01:24,698
What are you thinking?

5
00:01:26,461 --> 00:01:27,691
Nothing.

6
00:01:28,881 --> 00:01:30,372
Nothing what?

7
00:01:35,053 --> 00:01:37,054
Why are you like this...

8
00:01:37,806 --> 00:01:39,359
That's what I thought.

9
00:01:40,684 --> 00:01:42,215
And what about me?

10
00:01:43,145 --> 00:01:45,081
Why am I like this?

11
00:01:46,273 --> 00:01:47,742
That was my thought.

12
00:01:54,448 --> 00:01:56,950
Go back if you want to.

13
00:01:56,950 --> 00:01:59,506
I'll just live like this forever.

14
00:02:03,034 --> 00:02:04,456
Cho Yu Gyeom.

15
00:02:05,959 --> 00:02:08,960
Do you know when my mom ran away?

16
00:02:08,960 --> 00:02:10,084
I don't know.

17
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:15,558
When I was nine.

18
00:02:15,558 --> 00:02:17,929
I really liked that man.

19
00:02:17,929 --> 00:02:19,264
Sae Ryeong!

20
00:02:19,264 --> 00:02:21,080
Mister!

21
00:02:21,080 --> 00:02:22,434
Oh my.

22
00:02:22,434 --> 00:02:24,561
Idiot.

23
00:02:24,561 --> 00:02:27,324
Not even knowing he would run off with my mom.

24
00:02:30,567 --> 00:02:33,971
Seriously! If you ran,
you should have taken me.

25
00:02:33,971 --> 00:02:36,477
What's the point of running off without me?

26
00:02:37,824 --> 00:02:43,822
I acted so pitiful around him,
yet I was so scary to Mom.

27
00:02:44,790 --> 00:02:47,744
I dropped so many hints to take me along.

28
00:02:49,320 --> 00:02:51,011
What do you mean?

29
00:03:00,681 --> 00:03:02,398
Listen.

30
00:03:03,058 --> 00:03:06,858
I was already pitiful or scary
back then, Yu Gyeom.

31
00:03:07,813 --> 00:03:12,192
So you can't leave me.

32
00:03:12,192 --> 00:03:16,804
I don't plan on being left twice.

33
00:03:19,100 --> 00:03:20,629
Yu Gyeom.

34
00:03:20,629 --> 00:03:22,860
Don't you think that's too much?

35
00:03:26,456 --> 00:03:28,365
I'll let it go once.

36
00:03:28,980 --> 00:03:32,429
But if you leave me even one more time,

37
00:03:32,429 --> 00:03:36,133
I'm going to fall apart completely.

38
00:03:36,133 --> 00:03:37,175
Stop it.

39
00:03:37,175 --> 00:03:42,490
If I sink to the bottom and beg you
to save me with a desperate look...

40
00:03:43,140 --> 00:03:44,470
Cho Yu Gyeom.

41
00:03:45,223 --> 00:03:49,348
How scary and pitiful will I seem to you then?

42
00:03:49,348 --> 00:03:51,190
Hey.

43
00:03:51,190 --> 00:03:52,681
Sae Ryeong.

44
00:03:53,567 --> 00:03:55,467
The teacher wants you inside.

45
00:04:05,662 --> 00:04:09,300
[7. The Sky After the Rain]

46
00:04:12,043 --> 00:04:13,803
[Episode 7]

47
00:04:17,132 --> 00:04:18,728
[Staffing and Labor]

48
00:04:29,478 --> 00:04:31,771
Why did you come?

49
00:04:31,771 --> 00:04:35,317
I had to come to Seoul,
so I was coming straight to you.

50
00:04:35,317 --> 00:04:40,739
Well, I got the address wrong, so
last night I ended up in a really weird place.

51
00:04:40,739 --> 00:04:42,548
Where was it again?

52
00:04:42,548 --> 00:04:45,744
Ui-dong?

53
00:04:45,744 --> 00:04:48,167
It was so far away.

54
00:04:49,414 --> 00:04:53,544
But I bravely stayed at
a nearby motel for the night.

55
00:04:53,544 --> 00:04:56,969
Are Seoul motels always this empty?

56
00:04:56,969 --> 00:04:58,632
It's all machines.

57
00:04:58,632 --> 00:05:00,300
I was so surprised!

58
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:01,914
And there...

59
00:05:04,095 --> 00:05:05,680
Quick, tell me!

60
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:07,054
Stop chattering.

61
00:05:07,054 --> 00:05:08,327
My head hurts.

62
00:05:09,080 --> 00:05:15,273
And then I turned on the TV there,
and really, like this kept coming on!

63
00:05:15,273 --> 00:05:19,653
So I was totally flustered,
not knowing what to do, sweating like this...

64
00:05:19,653 --> 00:05:21,530
Hey, what the hell!

65
00:05:21,530 --> 00:05:24,992
I'll kill you!

66
00:05:24,992 --> 00:05:26,075
Die!

67
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:31,750
Seriously! I said I'll kill you! Die!

68
00:05:32,583 --> 00:05:35,342
- Why are you doing this?
- What's wrong?

69
00:05:37,254 --> 00:05:40,342
Dul Hee! Are you okay? Open your eyes!

70
00:05:40,342 --> 00:05:42,179
Are you okay? No!

71
00:05:42,179 --> 00:05:44,557
Help me!

72
00:05:45,179 --> 00:05:47,828
Dul Hee! Dul Hee!

73
00:05:51,101 --> 00:05:54,438
Vitals are stable, mental status alert,
and no neurological symptoms.

74
00:05:54,438 --> 00:05:58,358
A 3-cm laceration on the back of the head,
but no skull damage on palpation.

75
00:05:58,358 --> 00:06:00,694
To be safe, we'll do a brain CT and check.

76
00:06:00,694 --> 00:06:03,947
If it's fine, we'll suture,
book a follow-up, and discharge.

77
00:06:03,947 --> 00:06:08,451
However, the patient reports NRS 4 to 5
with RLQ rebound tenderness.

78
00:06:08,451 --> 00:06:10,495
She says pregnancy isn't possible.

79
00:06:10,495 --> 00:06:15,417
Still, I would do a urine hCG and abdominal CT
and review the images.

80
00:06:15,417 --> 00:06:16,710
Cho Dul Hee?

81
00:06:29,036 --> 00:06:30,401
Her guardian?

82
00:06:31,116 --> 00:06:32,373
Over there.

83
00:06:46,240 --> 00:06:47,417
Kid!

84
00:06:48,241 --> 00:06:49,993
You have grown a lot.

85
00:06:49,993 --> 00:06:51,576
Sir!

86
00:06:51,576 --> 00:06:53,496
How old are you? Did you graduate?

87
00:06:53,496 --> 00:06:54,581
Sir, why are you here?

88
00:06:54,581 --> 00:06:55,915
How are we meeting here?

89
00:06:55,915 --> 00:06:59,407
Of course your tutor from medical school
became a doctor.

90
00:06:59,407 --> 00:07:01,547
Sir, my sister!

91
00:07:01,547 --> 00:07:02,596
Yes, yes.

92
00:07:02,596 --> 00:07:04,472
Your sister is fine.

93
00:07:04,472 --> 00:07:06,305
Her head was cut.

94
00:07:06,305 --> 00:07:08,220
We stitched it. Three weeks and it'll heal.

95
00:07:08,220 --> 00:07:09,650
Yes, Sir.

96
00:07:09,650 --> 00:07:14,122
She keeps saying her stomach hurts,
so a CT and X-ray, and blood tests, too?

97
00:07:14,122 --> 00:07:15,651
Yes, Sir.

98
00:07:16,561 --> 00:07:17,989
Maybe appendicitis.

99
00:07:21,775 --> 00:07:23,930
Appendicitis is... you know the appendix?

100
00:07:23,930 --> 00:07:26,381
- Yes.
- Appendix. Surgery is all it needs.

101
00:07:26,381 --> 00:07:27,888
Then I'll do the surgery.

102
00:07:27,888 --> 00:07:29,032
Please operate, Sir.

103
00:07:29,032 --> 00:07:32,631
Right, to do surgery,
we need a guardian's signature.

104
00:07:36,248 --> 00:07:39,171
And you're not the guardian, kid, are you?

105
00:07:43,421 --> 00:07:45,834
She has both parents too.

106
00:07:45,834 --> 00:07:48,022
Just like you. Right?

107
00:07:57,853 --> 00:07:59,813
I like you.

108
00:07:59,813 --> 00:08:02,399
Please answer by tomorrow.

109
00:08:02,399 --> 00:08:04,597
It's fine if it's a no.

110
00:08:05,485 --> 00:08:09,198
I know you'll say no anyway.

111
00:08:09,948 --> 00:08:11,731
But you really have to...

112
00:08:12,512 --> 00:08:14,129
give me an answer.

113
00:08:15,045 --> 00:08:16,701
That way, I think I'll...

114
00:08:18,123 --> 00:08:20,513
be able to give up.

115
00:08:24,963 --> 00:08:28,000
[Entrance - Exit 2]

116
00:08:38,129 --> 00:08:40,020
Hello.

117
00:08:40,020 --> 00:08:43,939
I'm calling to answer your question.

118
00:08:43,939 --> 00:08:45,360
I...

119
00:08:52,198 --> 00:08:54,788
Kid. Did you have a brother?

120
00:08:54,788 --> 00:08:55,827
No, Sir.

121
00:08:55,827 --> 00:08:58,277
Then is your dad this young-looking?

122
00:08:58,277 --> 00:08:59,766
No, Sir. That's not it.

123
00:08:59,766 --> 00:09:01,458
Then who is this?

124
00:09:01,458 --> 00:09:03,972
Hello. I'm Kim Jung Yeon.

125
00:09:05,042 --> 00:09:06,195
Relationship?

126
00:09:06,195 --> 00:09:07,623
A friend.

127
00:09:10,175 --> 00:09:12,719
I asked for a guardian,
and you brought a friend?

128
00:09:12,719 --> 00:09:14,696
Well...

129
00:09:14,696 --> 00:09:16,656
Excuse me, but...

130
00:09:16,656 --> 00:09:19,184
Yes. Go ahead.

131
00:09:19,184 --> 00:09:25,170
Why do you call her kid and talk down to her?

132
00:09:25,170 --> 00:09:28,195
He was my tutor.

133
00:09:31,237 --> 00:09:36,326
Anyway, kid, a friend isn't a guardian, is he?

134
00:09:36,326 --> 00:09:40,156
And besides, he's not her friend.
He's your friend. Right?

135
00:09:40,156 --> 00:09:42,254
But...

136
00:09:42,254 --> 00:09:43,899
My mom...

137
00:09:44,793 --> 00:09:46,044
The phone call.

138
00:09:50,279 --> 00:09:52,519
Aren't you doing the surgery?

139
00:09:52,519 --> 00:09:54,679
I didn't explain how urgent the situation is.

140
00:09:54,679 --> 00:09:56,584
- You need surgery now--
- I'll call!

141
00:09:56,584 --> 00:09:58,741
Now. I'll call my mom.

142
00:10:09,703 --> 00:10:10,997
Cho Sam Hee.

143
00:10:10,997 --> 00:10:13,420
I'm busy, so be quick.

144
00:10:13,420 --> 00:10:15,699
Mom. Well...

145
00:10:15,699 --> 00:10:17,254
I...

146
00:10:18,785 --> 00:10:22,065
I met Dul Hee...

147
00:10:23,016 --> 00:10:25,546
- What?
- No, that's not it.

148
00:10:25,546 --> 00:10:30,006
But right now, Dul Hee is...

149
00:10:30,754 --> 00:10:33,132
Cho Sam Hee, she's not my daughter.

150
00:10:33,132 --> 00:10:34,296
I'm busy. Hanging up.

151
00:10:34,296 --> 00:10:37,304
- Mom, it's not that, right now...
- Let me talk to her.

152
00:10:37,304 --> 00:10:40,143
Ma'am. This is Jeong Ju.

153
00:10:40,143 --> 00:10:42,737
Yes, do you remember me?

154
00:10:42,737 --> 00:10:45,229
Yes, the med student.

155
00:10:45,229 --> 00:10:48,303
Yes. I'm a doctor now.

156
00:10:48,303 --> 00:10:52,233
Your daughter, Cho Dul Hee, is my patient.

157
00:10:57,179 --> 00:10:58,879
It's appendicitis.

158
00:10:58,879 --> 00:11:03,037
It's the appendix,
and it needs immediate surgery.

159
00:11:03,037 --> 00:11:06,298
But a parent has to sign for the surgery.

160
00:11:06,298 --> 00:11:11,676
If her parents were gone or unreachable,
we wouldn't look this hard.

161
00:11:11,676 --> 00:11:13,581
But you're alive.

162
00:11:13,581 --> 00:11:15,927
You're even on the phone with me.

163
00:11:18,754 --> 00:11:22,773
Ma'am. Please don't think
appendicitis is nothing.

164
00:11:22,773 --> 00:11:28,178
She could die in surgery,
so come to Seoul and sign right now.

165
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:31,930
It's two hours by train.

166
00:11:31,930 --> 00:11:38,222
As you know, untreated appendicitis
can lead to peritonitis, then sepsis--

167
00:11:39,292 --> 00:11:40,618
Hello?

168
00:11:42,285 --> 00:11:44,826
Sir, is my sister really in that much danger?

169
00:11:44,826 --> 00:11:46,874
- Really...
- Kid.

170
00:11:46,874 --> 00:11:49,214
Your mom's coming. Don't worry.

171
00:11:50,418 --> 00:11:51,991
I'm going into surgery.

172
00:11:51,991 --> 00:11:54,132
You said no surgery until Mom comes.

173
00:11:54,132 --> 00:11:56,379
Of course that was a bluff.

174
00:11:56,379 --> 00:11:57,945
- Hee Seok!
- Yes, Sir.

175
00:11:57,945 --> 00:12:00,814
Contact anesthesia and get an operating room.
It's an emergency.

176
00:12:00,814 --> 00:12:02,097
Yes, understood.

177
00:12:02,097 --> 00:12:03,377
See you later.

178
00:12:12,274 --> 00:12:15,526
If he's doing the surgery,
I think she'll be fine.

179
00:12:15,526 --> 00:12:21,012
But earlier, Sir said death and
peritonitis and appendicitis.

180
00:12:21,012 --> 00:12:23,034
He said so many things.

181
00:12:23,034 --> 00:12:25,844
I think he was just scaring her.

182
00:12:25,844 --> 00:12:27,589
To get your mom to come.

183
00:12:30,083 --> 00:12:32,502
I think she'll really be fine.

184
00:12:32,502 --> 00:12:34,379
Don't worry.

185
00:12:34,379 --> 00:12:35,965
Right?

186
00:12:35,965 --> 00:12:37,447
I guess so.

187
00:12:39,468 --> 00:12:41,125
By the way,

188
00:12:42,012 --> 00:12:46,562
about what you asked me earlier,
I'm going to answer now.

189
00:12:48,832 --> 00:12:49,971
No.

190
00:12:49,971 --> 00:12:51,563
Shut up.

191
00:12:51,563 --> 00:12:54,995
Saying that now would be pouring oil
on a raging fire, okay?

192
00:13:00,364 --> 00:13:02,147
Have you eaten?

193
00:13:05,920 --> 00:13:07,352
No.

194
00:14:29,869 --> 00:14:32,170
I don't want to.

195
00:14:32,170 --> 00:14:34,292
I won't. Never.

196
00:14:34,292 --> 00:14:37,420
I'll never break up.

197
00:15:36,052 --> 00:15:39,672
Hey, Lee Won Bae. Now you too?

198
00:15:39,672 --> 00:15:41,161
Hi.

199
00:15:42,067 --> 00:15:44,820
Hey, what happened to Kim Jin Mi?

200
00:15:44,820 --> 00:15:47,501
She should be locked up in a hospital.

201
00:15:47,501 --> 00:15:49,387
I really thought she was crazy.

202
00:15:49,387 --> 00:15:50,796
What's with the water balloon?

203
00:15:50,796 --> 00:15:53,980
Hey, I heard she'll be suspended.

204
00:15:54,745 --> 00:15:56,732
Hey, but Sung Sae Ryeong...

205
00:15:57,666 --> 00:15:59,597
She has nothing at all.

206
00:15:59,597 --> 00:16:03,713
Sae Ryeong's side can stay quiet,
the teacher saw. It goes to committee.

207
00:16:03,713 --> 00:16:05,672
There's more than one witness.

208
00:16:05,672 --> 00:16:08,221
But what's with Sae Ryeong and Yu Gyeom?

209
00:16:08,221 --> 00:16:09,421
Are they dating again?

210
00:16:09,421 --> 00:16:11,274
Hey, they held hands.

211
00:16:11,274 --> 00:16:12,313
On purpose.

212
00:16:12,313 --> 00:16:15,558
I know. What is that? It's so over the top.

213
00:16:15,558 --> 00:16:18,131
What else? Can't you tell?

214
00:16:19,752 --> 00:16:21,450
Sae Ryeong, you're here?

215
00:16:22,899 --> 00:16:25,402
Sae Ryeong, you okay? Get home all right?

216
00:16:25,402 --> 00:16:28,530
Right. Didn't you catch a cold? I was worried.

217
00:16:28,530 --> 00:16:30,730
I'm fine. It's nothing.

218
00:16:30,730 --> 00:16:33,380
- Really, it doesn't hurt?
- Yes, I'm fine.

219
00:16:41,671 --> 00:16:46,048
I thought I would sleep for an hour
no matter what and wake up.

220
00:16:46,048 --> 00:16:47,090
I'm sorry.

221
00:16:47,090 --> 00:16:49,811
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.
What do I do? I apologize.

222
00:16:51,428 --> 00:16:53,644
Does it hurt? It hurts, right?

223
00:16:54,765 --> 00:16:56,431
It hurts.

224
00:17:00,437 --> 00:17:03,357
I have been like this for over seven hours.

225
00:17:03,357 --> 00:17:05,274
Seven hours?

226
00:17:05,274 --> 00:17:06,720
What do I do?

227
00:17:06,720 --> 00:17:08,471
Let's go to the hospital.

228
00:17:08,471 --> 00:17:09,885
This is the hospital.

229
00:17:09,885 --> 00:17:11,262
Which department should I go to?

230
00:17:11,262 --> 00:17:13,072
Hospital, quick!

231
00:17:13,783 --> 00:17:15,348
It's not that bad.

232
00:17:15,348 --> 00:17:17,161
Then what do I do?

233
00:17:17,161 --> 00:17:21,484
Well, I'll at least buy you a meal.

234
00:17:22,464 --> 00:17:24,092
- Just that?
- Well...

235
00:17:24,092 --> 00:17:26,834
Then a meal! And coffee! My treat!

236
00:17:27,850 --> 00:17:29,711
And I'll buy ice cream too.

237
00:17:32,253 --> 00:17:33,972
Okay.

238
00:17:33,972 --> 00:17:35,597
Go in first.

239
00:17:35,597 --> 00:17:37,301
Your mother came at dawn.

240
00:17:37,301 --> 00:17:39,393
Really? My mom?

241
00:17:39,393 --> 00:17:40,421
Yes.

242
00:17:40,421 --> 00:17:42,095
See your mother first.

243
00:17:42,095 --> 00:17:46,494
Then have a meal, coffee, and ice cream.

244
00:17:46,494 --> 00:17:47,546
Okay.

245
00:17:53,740 --> 00:17:55,206
Get out!

246
00:17:55,206 --> 00:17:56,421
I understood.

247
00:17:56,421 --> 00:17:57,995
"Get out," right?

248
00:17:59,621 --> 00:18:01,344
Dul Hee. Dul Hee.

249
00:18:03,398 --> 00:18:07,260
I didn't want to come either.

250
00:18:07,260 --> 00:18:10,761
I came because they said a guardian was needed.

251
00:18:12,174 --> 00:18:15,025
Did you tell her?

252
00:18:15,888 --> 00:18:17,638
Did you tell this woman?

253
00:18:17,638 --> 00:18:21,576
The hospital said they can't operate
without a guardian, so...

254
00:18:22,962 --> 00:18:25,647
Then don't do the surgery!

255
00:18:25,647 --> 00:18:27,846
It's already done.

256
00:18:27,846 --> 00:18:29,593
Don't bother saying that.

257
00:18:31,695 --> 00:18:32,984
Get out!

258
00:18:35,908 --> 00:18:37,367
I said get out!

259
00:18:37,367 --> 00:18:38,572
Fine.

260
00:18:39,285 --> 00:18:40,913
I'm leaving.

261
00:18:40,913 --> 00:18:44,575
Mom, wait. Please, please.

262
00:18:46,156 --> 00:18:49,097
Dul Hee, listen to me, okay?

263
00:18:49,097 --> 00:18:51,151
That was really fast.

264
00:18:54,009 --> 00:18:56,135
What is that?

265
00:18:56,135 --> 00:18:58,683
I understood that. "What is that?"

266
00:19:00,379 --> 00:19:02,228
Get out!

267
00:19:03,003 --> 00:19:04,272
Now!

268
00:19:13,277 --> 00:19:15,334
You're full of energy.

269
00:19:15,334 --> 00:19:17,305
You're alive, Cho Dul Hee.

270
00:19:21,156 --> 00:19:24,581
Hey, it's that girl. Her again.

271
00:19:24,581 --> 00:19:26,696
Seriously, how pitiful.

272
00:19:26,696 --> 00:19:28,541
Seoul's nothing special.

273
00:19:36,537 --> 00:19:39,015
How sad for her.

274
00:20:25,015 --> 00:20:27,394
Making one million in a year.

275
00:20:27,394 --> 00:20:29,649
Now, what does this sentence mean?

276
00:20:29,649 --> 00:20:32,440
"Making one million in a year."

277
00:20:32,440 --> 00:20:34,984
It starts with a gerund.

278
00:20:34,984 --> 00:20:37,779
But there's the word "but" after it.

279
00:20:37,779 --> 00:20:40,115
[Cho Yu Gyeom]
So what comes next?

280
00:20:40,115 --> 00:20:42,863
A sentence that differs from the one before.

281
00:20:42,863 --> 00:20:46,205
So, nothing in the preceding line.

282
00:20:46,205 --> 00:20:47,872
Then what is "preceding"?

283
00:20:47,872 --> 00:20:50,622
It means what came before.

284
00:20:50,622 --> 00:20:52,172
Do you understand?

285
00:21:08,477 --> 00:21:10,287
There was nothing.

286
00:21:11,313 --> 00:21:14,772
You earn one million in a year.

287
00:21:23,856 --> 00:21:26,453
The professor will be making rounds soon.

288
00:21:26,453 --> 00:21:29,883
He'll be delighted to see
the state of this room.

289
00:21:31,792 --> 00:21:34,356
Hello, Ma'am. How have you been?

290
00:21:34,962 --> 00:21:37,236
How have you been, young Jeong Ju?

291
00:21:44,977 --> 00:21:48,140
And here's the lively Cho Dul Hee.

292
00:21:48,140 --> 00:21:49,512
I see you're strong.

293
00:21:49,512 --> 00:21:54,047
But if you keep moving like that,
the stitches will tear and you'll need surgery.

294
00:21:55,556 --> 00:21:56,856
Though that won't happen.

295
00:21:56,856 --> 00:21:59,361
I put in two or three staples.

296
00:21:59,361 --> 00:22:02,509
Oppa? Why are you here?

297
00:22:02,509 --> 00:22:05,784
Hey. What do you mean, "Oppa"?

298
00:22:05,784 --> 00:22:08,724
"Doctor," I told you to call me Doctor.

299
00:22:08,724 --> 00:22:11,747
Ma'am, she always calls me "Oppa" like that,

300
00:22:11,747 --> 00:22:14,333
I don't know any sign language,
but I know "Oppa".

301
00:22:14,333 --> 00:22:15,967
What?

302
00:22:16,877 --> 00:22:21,216
I already told her I can't sign.

303
00:22:21,216 --> 00:22:24,310
She still stubbornly signs to me.

304
00:22:24,310 --> 00:22:25,721
Ma'am.

305
00:22:25,721 --> 00:22:31,537
Dul Hee gets out in two days,
but what comes next is a problem.

306
00:22:31,537 --> 00:22:36,322
What else would I use but sign!
Don't talk to that woman.

307
00:22:36,322 --> 00:22:38,247
What's she saying, kid?

308
00:22:40,756 --> 00:22:43,211
Don't talk to Mom.

309
00:22:44,363 --> 00:22:47,367
Then who do I talk to? Your mom's the guardian.

310
00:22:47,367 --> 00:22:48,471
Talk to me.

311
00:22:48,471 --> 00:22:51,989
I'm my own guardian.

312
00:22:53,896 --> 00:22:55,596
She's her own guardian.

313
00:22:56,875 --> 00:22:59,670
That's not for you to decide.

314
00:22:59,670 --> 00:23:01,988
You, get out.

315
00:23:03,132 --> 00:23:05,135
"You"?

316
00:23:05,135 --> 00:23:08,496
Ma'am, did you see? She called me "you."

317
00:23:08,496 --> 00:23:12,215
That's why I quit tutoring her. It was so hard.

318
00:23:12,215 --> 00:23:13,519
Ma'am.

319
00:23:13,519 --> 00:23:15,015
Yes.

320
00:23:16,637 --> 00:23:18,941
I said get out, all of you!

321
00:23:22,546 --> 00:23:24,096
Excuse me.

322
00:23:24,096 --> 00:23:25,909
She says everyone leave.

323
00:23:26,782 --> 00:23:29,158
You're picking it up... Ma'am!

324
00:23:29,158 --> 00:23:30,189
Wait one moment.

325
00:23:30,189 --> 00:23:33,971
Anyway, Dul Hee only needs two more days here.

326
00:23:33,971 --> 00:23:39,673
But now she can't go back
to where she lived in that state.

327
00:23:39,673 --> 00:23:44,356
Because the one who did that
to her head lives there.

328
00:23:44,356 --> 00:23:46,236
Right, kid?

329
00:23:46,236 --> 00:23:47,630
Yes, Sir.

330
00:23:48,469 --> 00:23:50,804
She lives in the same building
as that criminal.

331
00:23:50,804 --> 00:23:54,471
And he is out to kill Cho Dul Hee now.

332
00:23:54,471 --> 00:23:56,676
Right, kid?

333
00:23:56,676 --> 00:23:57,769
Yes, Sir.

334
00:23:57,769 --> 00:23:59,378
So here's the thing.

335
00:24:00,751 --> 00:24:04,637
I would like you to take her home.

336
00:24:16,869 --> 00:24:18,086
I...

337
00:24:19,754 --> 00:24:22,624
I can't take her, Jeong Ju.

338
00:24:25,422 --> 00:24:26,741
Right.

339
00:24:26,741 --> 00:24:29,967
You're Dul Hee's mother.

340
00:24:30,790 --> 00:24:32,445
No.

341
00:24:32,445 --> 00:24:34,383
I'm not her mother.

342
00:24:35,640 --> 00:24:38,584
I came because they needed a guardian.

343
00:24:40,284 --> 00:24:43,429
As you saw, I'm not her guardian.

344
00:24:43,429 --> 00:24:45,160
So, Jeong Ju...

345
00:24:45,160 --> 00:24:48,121
From now on, even if she's
rushed to the hospital...

346
00:24:49,179 --> 00:24:51,325
Please don't call me.

347
00:24:51,325 --> 00:24:53,958
Contact her father instead.

348
00:24:55,579 --> 00:24:57,737
I don't have a daughter like that.

349
00:25:09,248 --> 00:25:11,350
I don't see your wife.

350
00:25:12,346 --> 00:25:13,430
Yes.

351
00:25:14,664 --> 00:25:18,277
My wife had family matters,
so she went to Seoul for a bit.

352
00:25:18,277 --> 00:25:19,984
To her family's home?

353
00:25:20,614 --> 00:25:23,416
Did something happen?

354
00:25:23,416 --> 00:25:25,636
I don't think it's that serious.

355
00:25:27,317 --> 00:25:28,387
Jae Jin.

356
00:25:28,387 --> 00:25:29,535
Yes, Father.

357
00:25:29,535 --> 00:25:31,839
Tell your wife.

358
00:25:31,839 --> 00:25:35,157
Unless it's serious, a wife
shouldn't visit her parents.

359
00:25:36,578 --> 00:25:39,054
- Yes, Father. I'll tell her.
- Okay.

360
00:25:39,054 --> 00:25:40,375
I'm sorry.

361
00:25:42,979 --> 00:25:46,416
And about Hui Gyeong,

362
00:25:48,224 --> 00:25:52,928
tell her to come and go
when Yu Gyeom isn't here.

363
00:25:52,928 --> 00:25:55,639
I'm not saying don't come.

364
00:25:56,682 --> 00:26:00,197
Just make sure she doesn't run into Yu Gyeom.

365
00:26:01,170 --> 00:26:05,962
But Father, Hui Gyeong comes to see Yu Gyeom--

366
00:26:05,962 --> 00:26:07,896
Do as I say!

367
00:26:13,177 --> 00:26:14,586
Hello?

368
00:26:15,365 --> 00:26:16,394
What?

369
00:26:16,394 --> 00:26:18,345
The machine broke down?

370
00:26:20,532 --> 00:26:23,179
I'll ask my father and call you back.

371
00:26:23,179 --> 00:26:24,448
Yes.

372
00:26:46,481 --> 00:26:48,964
What's that? Can I try it?

373
00:26:55,199 --> 00:26:56,906
Seriously.

374
00:26:59,535 --> 00:27:01,624
Just tell me not to, then.

375
00:27:01,624 --> 00:27:03,999
I'm still with Kim Ha Yeon.

376
00:27:03,999 --> 00:27:05,052
What?

377
00:27:07,598 --> 00:27:10,097
I didn't go back to you.

378
00:27:10,097 --> 00:27:11,492
So...

379
00:27:14,360 --> 00:27:16,304
Ease up.

380
00:27:16,304 --> 00:27:18,702
Before your pitiful act stops working.

381
00:27:44,839 --> 00:27:46,119
Yu Gyeom.

382
00:27:56,248 --> 00:27:58,886
I want to talk to you.

383
00:27:58,886 --> 00:28:00,638
Okay.

384
00:28:00,638 --> 00:28:02,316
Then where...

385
00:28:03,464 --> 00:28:04,930
Hey! Cho Yu Gyeom!

386
00:28:04,930 --> 00:28:07,671
Assembly! Hurry!

387
00:28:09,779 --> 00:28:12,344
I'll wait here. Go.

388
00:28:12,344 --> 00:28:17,720
Well, practice might run late.

389
00:28:18,604 --> 00:28:20,529
Then, 9:30 p.m.

390
00:28:20,529 --> 00:28:22,494
I'll wait at the beach.

391
00:28:22,494 --> 00:28:24,524
That works, right?

392
00:28:24,524 --> 00:28:27,124
Hey! Hurry up!

393
00:28:27,124 --> 00:28:28,311
Go on.

394
00:28:55,569 --> 00:28:57,447
How old are you?

395
00:28:58,487 --> 00:29:00,249
I'm 21.

396
00:29:01,241 --> 00:29:03,154
The most tiring age.

397
00:29:07,247 --> 00:29:09,068
Kid's boyfriend?

398
00:29:10,424 --> 00:29:12,459
No. Not at all.

399
00:29:12,459 --> 00:29:13,639
Then what were you?

400
00:29:14,249 --> 00:29:15,641
A friend.

401
00:29:21,303 --> 00:29:22,871
Then, Sir...

402
00:29:23,553 --> 00:29:25,265
That Dul Hee?

403
00:29:25,265 --> 00:29:27,297
What's your relationship with her?

404
00:29:30,854 --> 00:29:32,847
My student. Like Sam Hee...

405
00:29:34,606 --> 00:29:36,175
No?

406
00:29:36,175 --> 00:29:38,542
They didn't look alike at all.

407
00:29:44,960 --> 00:29:46,906
You're sharp.

408
00:29:48,288 --> 00:29:49,884
What?

409
00:29:49,884 --> 00:29:51,375
Hey.

410
00:29:51,375 --> 00:29:54,095
Cho Dul Hee is a scary kid.

411
00:29:54,095 --> 00:29:58,148
When I tutored her, she liked me...

412
00:29:58,148 --> 00:30:01,604
She would open her shirt and
lunge at me, and I would run.

413
00:30:01,604 --> 00:30:04,743
I'm truly scared of her.

414
00:30:05,931 --> 00:30:08,117
You didn't seem scared at all.

415
00:30:09,068 --> 00:30:12,462
No. I'm so scared of her, really.

416
00:30:12,462 --> 00:30:13,730
Sir.

417
00:30:13,730 --> 00:30:15,298
Kid.

418
00:30:22,531 --> 00:30:25,158
So how did it go? Your family's soap opera.

419
00:30:25,158 --> 00:30:28,994
I ran away because I would be
destroyed in the middle.

420
00:30:28,994 --> 00:30:30,780
That was a very wise choice.

421
00:30:30,780 --> 00:30:32,789
Good for you, kid.

422
00:30:32,789 --> 00:30:34,574
You should eat. Want some?

423
00:30:34,574 --> 00:30:36,339
No. I can get it myself.

424
00:30:36,339 --> 00:30:39,173
No, I'm already done eating.

425
00:30:39,173 --> 00:30:41,091
I'll bring it.

426
00:30:41,091 --> 00:30:45,366
[Staff cafeteria]

427
00:30:48,144 --> 00:30:49,964
He seems to like you.

428
00:30:49,964 --> 00:30:51,195
What?

429
00:30:51,195 --> 00:30:52,575
No.

430
00:30:52,575 --> 00:30:54,874
He doesn't like me.

431
00:30:56,104 --> 00:30:58,095
I like him.

432
00:30:58,095 --> 00:31:00,282
And I'll get dumped today, Sir.

433
00:31:01,695 --> 00:31:04,475
Sorry. I'm hopeless when it comes to romance.

434
00:31:07,824 --> 00:31:09,664
You must have been so hungry.

435
00:31:09,664 --> 00:31:11,682
It's my first meal today.

436
00:31:12,924 --> 00:31:13,997
Hey.

437
00:31:14,666 --> 00:31:17,691
Is your sister really not welcome anywhere?

438
00:31:17,691 --> 00:31:19,842
Yes, Sir.

439
00:31:19,842 --> 00:31:20,956
No,

440
00:31:22,006 --> 00:31:25,480
What good life did she live
to have nowhere to go?

441
00:31:25,480 --> 00:31:27,504
Sir, should I buy you coffee?

442
00:31:27,504 --> 00:31:28,716
No.

443
00:31:32,974 --> 00:31:34,628
How long will she live so well?

444
00:31:34,628 --> 00:31:37,494
You still like cafe latte, right, Sir?

445
00:31:40,317 --> 00:31:42,446
- Buy me one?
- Yes.

446
00:31:43,987 --> 00:31:45,764
Get out.

447
00:31:46,678 --> 00:31:49,164
I said get lost!

448
00:31:49,164 --> 00:31:51,150
Go to Cho Yu Gyeom.

449
00:31:54,122 --> 00:31:55,785
I'm leaving.

450
00:31:56,373 --> 00:31:59,622
You don't need to worry about me.

451
00:32:02,937 --> 00:32:06,824
People told me I left that house?

452
00:32:06,824 --> 00:32:08,301
Right.

453
00:32:08,301 --> 00:32:11,126
You left on your own.

454
00:32:11,126 --> 00:32:12,818
Who kicked you out?

455
00:32:19,729 --> 00:32:21,273
No.

456
00:32:21,273 --> 00:32:27,237
That house raises girls to
become maids when they turn 20.

457
00:32:27,237 --> 00:32:32,327
I couldn't become a maid,
so I had no choice but to leave.

458
00:32:32,327 --> 00:32:37,157
I couldn't stay there
if I wasn't a maid, right?

459
00:32:39,001 --> 00:32:40,205
Right.

460
00:32:40,961 --> 00:32:42,301
I...

461
00:32:43,364 --> 00:32:46,479
I like living as a maid.

462
00:32:46,479 --> 00:32:50,475
Better than wandering like you.

463
00:32:50,475 --> 00:32:52,391
Do you like it?

464
00:32:55,432 --> 00:32:57,846
Mom.

465
00:32:57,846 --> 00:33:00,944
You must think
you're living a pretty good life.

466
00:33:04,024 --> 00:33:05,777
Right.

467
00:33:05,777 --> 00:33:10,718
Mom, surely you know you're a maid?

468
00:33:13,003 --> 00:33:14,169
Mom.

469
00:33:15,295 --> 00:33:17,706
Mom. You're a maid.

470
00:33:17,706 --> 00:33:20,475
You only leave that house when you die.

471
00:33:25,364 --> 00:33:26,748
Cho Dul Hee.

472
00:33:31,303 --> 00:33:36,517
You carry designer bags
and wear designer clothes.

473
00:33:36,517 --> 00:33:40,751
You ride around in nice cars.

474
00:33:40,751 --> 00:33:44,254
You give things to people who grovel.

475
00:33:44,254 --> 00:33:50,254
Did you think that made you
the lady of that town?

476
00:33:50,254 --> 00:33:52,087
Don't make me laugh.

477
00:33:52,087 --> 00:33:55,533
You're just a maid.

478
00:33:55,533 --> 00:34:01,519
A lady on the outside, a maid inside.

479
00:34:04,336 --> 00:34:05,893
Are you done?

480
00:34:07,464 --> 00:34:11,892
You are a total wreck.

481
00:34:26,754 --> 00:34:30,200
[Gym]

482
00:34:53,001 --> 00:34:56,224
All right, good work, everyone. Dismissed.

483
00:34:56,224 --> 00:34:57,950
Good work, Sir.

484
00:35:04,438 --> 00:35:05,808
Cho Yu Gyeom.

485
00:35:34,883 --> 00:35:36,178
I have to go.

486
00:35:36,178 --> 00:35:37,408
Where?

487
00:35:38,720 --> 00:35:40,371
Call me later.

488
00:35:40,371 --> 00:35:41,876
Yu Gyeom. Listen.

489
00:35:41,876 --> 00:35:45,311
You don't find me scary or pitiful enough yet.

490
00:35:46,939 --> 00:35:51,424
That's why you still act tough
about not breaking up with Kim Ha Yeon.

491
00:35:51,424 --> 00:35:53,721
You broke up with Kim Ha Yeon.

492
00:35:53,721 --> 00:35:55,697
You're the only one who doesn't know.

493
00:35:55,697 --> 00:35:57,699
Kim Ha Yeon gave up on you too.

494
00:35:57,699 --> 00:35:59,462
Hey.

495
00:35:59,462 --> 00:36:02,084
That's not for you to decide. Okay?

496
00:36:02,084 --> 00:36:07,543
Yu Gyeom, I have always told you, let's talk.

497
00:36:07,543 --> 00:36:09,308
You know,

498
00:36:10,224 --> 00:36:13,106
I really wanted to talk to you.

499
00:36:15,084 --> 00:36:18,701
Like the story about my mom
I told you yesterday.

500
00:36:18,701 --> 00:36:20,280
And there's my dad too.

501
00:36:20,280 --> 00:36:21,723
Why?

502
00:36:21,723 --> 00:36:24,498
Because those stories make me pity you?

503
00:36:25,310 --> 00:36:26,700
Then I'll...

504
00:36:27,644 --> 00:36:30,343
never leave your side?

505
00:36:30,343 --> 00:36:32,179
Right. Yes, Cho Yu Gyeom.

506
00:36:32,179 --> 00:36:33,274
You're smart.

507
00:36:33,274 --> 00:36:35,175
Yes, you're pitiful.

508
00:36:35,988 --> 00:36:38,031
Right. So forget Kim Ha Yeon.

509
00:36:38,031 --> 00:36:39,084
She's not pitiful.

510
00:36:39,084 --> 00:36:41,795
Right. You're truly pitiful.

511
00:36:41,795 --> 00:36:45,836
But the problem is I don't like you.

512
00:36:47,624 --> 00:36:48,753
What?

513
00:36:48,753 --> 00:36:50,677
I liked you at first.

514
00:36:52,273 --> 00:36:53,471
But not now.

515
00:36:53,471 --> 00:36:54,956
Not even a little.

516
00:36:54,956 --> 00:36:56,302
No.

517
00:36:56,302 --> 00:36:59,717
You came to me every time
I was in a pitiful situation.

518
00:36:59,717 --> 00:37:01,719
So I thought about it.

519
00:37:01,719 --> 00:37:06,768
Kim Jin Mi made a fuss at me
and I don't think it was that pitiful to you.

520
00:37:06,768 --> 00:37:08,852
What are you talking about?

521
00:37:08,852 --> 00:37:13,575
You never wanted to see my body.

522
00:37:13,575 --> 00:37:15,567
You wouldn't even be curious. Yu Gyeom.

523
00:37:15,567 --> 00:37:17,272
What are you doing?

524
00:37:27,372 --> 00:37:29,335
This isn't all there is.

525
00:37:34,081 --> 00:37:36,138
There's some here too.

526
00:37:36,138 --> 00:37:37,813
What is this...

527
00:37:40,871 --> 00:37:42,462
You know.

528
00:37:43,639 --> 00:37:47,850
When it gets late at night,
I hate myself so much?

529
00:37:48,766 --> 00:37:50,312
What?

530
00:37:50,312 --> 00:37:54,741
Every time, I carved cuts
into my body like this.

531
00:38:00,656 --> 00:38:03,049
Will you still leave me?

532
00:38:07,287 --> 00:38:08,471
Answer me.

533
00:38:08,471 --> 00:38:10,282
Will you leave me?

534
00:38:14,434 --> 00:38:16,022
I really...

535
00:38:16,861 --> 00:38:18,803
Sung Sae Ryeong, you...

536
00:38:18,803 --> 00:38:22,788
If you don't leave me,
I have a reason to love myself.

537
00:38:22,788 --> 00:38:25,060
But if you leave me...

538
00:38:28,824 --> 00:38:31,039
I have no need to love myself. Yu Gyeom.

539
00:38:31,039 --> 00:38:32,072
Stop it!

540
00:38:32,072 --> 00:38:33,137
Answer me.

541
00:38:33,137 --> 00:38:35,795
Will you leave me even so?

542
00:38:36,441 --> 00:38:39,439
Please stop doing crazy things.
This won't work.

543
00:38:48,787 --> 00:38:50,998
I knew you would be like this.

544
00:38:50,998 --> 00:38:55,333
You know, I knew I would come this far.

545
00:38:55,333 --> 00:38:58,236
How can you not feel sorry for me?

546
00:38:58,236 --> 00:39:02,339
How can you abandon me like this? How?

547
00:39:05,168 --> 00:39:06,779
How...

548
00:39:09,288 --> 00:39:12,556
can you not love me? Yu Gyeom.

549
00:39:15,144 --> 00:39:17,316
Please. Stop doing strange things. I...

550
00:39:17,316 --> 00:39:19,943
It may be very strange to you, but not to me.

551
00:39:19,943 --> 00:39:22,637
I'm desperate. That's why. Understand?

552
00:39:39,421 --> 00:39:40,512
Sung Sae...

553
00:39:40,512 --> 00:39:41,664
Hey.

554
00:39:46,968 --> 00:39:48,889
Hey, why aren't you coming out?

555
00:39:48,889 --> 00:39:51,514
Right. I'll pass out waiting...

556
00:40:17,707 --> 00:40:19,066
How do I...

557
00:40:20,588 --> 00:40:22,568
Look at this.

558
00:40:22,568 --> 00:40:27,963
Look at how cruel the world you gave me is.

559
00:40:28,804 --> 00:40:31,598
Sae Ryeong, no! Open your eyes!

560
00:40:31,598 --> 00:40:33,207
Please!

561
00:40:34,849 --> 00:40:36,054
What's with Sae Ryeong?

562
00:40:36,054 --> 00:40:37,220
Won Bae, get a teacher!

563
00:40:37,220 --> 00:40:40,232
I said get him now, you idiot!

564
00:40:40,232 --> 00:40:42,063
Sir! Sir!

565
00:40:43,709 --> 00:40:46,722
Shin Seung Chan. Call 119, please!

566
00:40:47,768 --> 00:40:48,812
Hey.

567
00:40:51,754 --> 00:40:54,077
Hey, what's wrong?

568
00:40:54,077 --> 00:40:56,037
Hey. Hold on.

569
00:40:56,037 --> 00:40:57,955
Cho Yu Gyeom, what's wrong with her?

570
00:40:57,955 --> 00:40:59,586
Let go of her.

571
00:41:00,294 --> 00:41:03,002
Sae Ryeong... she used that...

572
00:41:03,002 --> 00:41:04,715
her wrist...

573
00:41:05,936 --> 00:41:09,577
to cut her wrist...

574
00:41:16,935 --> 00:41:18,476
But...

575
00:41:19,730 --> 00:41:21,747
Yes. Go ahead.

576
00:41:22,483 --> 00:41:26,218
Why does your mother hate your sister so much?

577
00:41:29,990 --> 00:41:31,657
Because she left home.

578
00:41:33,368 --> 00:41:38,144
Even so, saying not to look for her
next time she's hurt.

579
00:41:39,374 --> 00:41:43,348
Well, my family is a bit complicated.

580
00:41:47,007 --> 00:41:48,991
Grandfather is strict too.

581
00:41:50,610 --> 00:41:52,202
Yes, Grandpa!

582
00:41:53,428 --> 00:41:55,429
I'm taking a walk right now.

583
00:41:55,429 --> 00:41:56,522
Yes.

584
00:41:57,212 --> 00:41:59,763
Of course! I'm coming down today.

585
00:41:59,763 --> 00:42:01,587
Yes!

586
00:42:03,565 --> 00:42:05,319
Right.

587
00:42:06,568 --> 00:42:08,617
My grandfather is strict, too.

588
00:42:09,603 --> 00:42:11,764
It doesn't seem like it at all.

589
00:42:12,658 --> 00:42:15,992
With me, my grandfather's a pushover.

590
00:42:15,992 --> 00:42:17,568
A pushover?

591
00:42:17,568 --> 00:42:19,372
But not with my mom.

592
00:42:19,372 --> 00:42:23,859
So when Mom comes to Seoul,
Grandpa gets really angry.

593
00:42:24,730 --> 00:42:27,008
But his granddaughter is sick.

594
00:42:27,008 --> 00:42:29,729
That doesn't work on him at all.

595
00:42:32,063 --> 00:42:34,058
That's a bit curious.

596
00:42:34,917 --> 00:42:36,637
Yes.

597
00:42:36,637 --> 00:42:39,261
There's a lot more curious stuff.

598
00:42:42,894 --> 00:42:45,173
Speaking of which, Jung Yeon.

599
00:42:45,173 --> 00:42:46,543
Yes.

600
00:42:47,294 --> 00:42:49,766
You can give me your answer now.

601
00:42:50,865 --> 00:42:53,603
The answer to my question.

602
00:42:59,368 --> 00:43:01,353
I'm ready to hear it now.

603
00:43:01,353 --> 00:43:05,287
Even if you pour oil on my heart,
it won't catch fire.

604
00:43:06,111 --> 00:43:10,411
I'm much better now, and I'm fully prepared.

605
00:43:11,086 --> 00:43:12,316
Okay.

606
00:43:14,178 --> 00:43:15,681
Let's do it.

607
00:43:17,511 --> 00:43:19,274
Do what...

608
00:43:19,274 --> 00:43:20,764
Let's meet.

609
00:43:21,602 --> 00:43:22,709
What?

610
00:43:23,720 --> 00:43:26,106
Let's try dating. You and me.

611
00:43:26,106 --> 00:43:27,865
I'm fine with it.

612
00:43:36,308 --> 00:43:38,354
What happened?

613
00:43:38,354 --> 00:43:42,658
They say she suddenly cut her wrist
with a razor, right in front of him.

614
00:43:44,859 --> 00:43:47,428
Seung Chan, look after him.

615
00:43:47,428 --> 00:43:48,942
Yes.

616
00:43:48,942 --> 00:43:50,628
What about Sae Ryeong?

617
00:43:50,628 --> 00:43:53,297
Sae Ryeong? She's in surgery.
It had better go well.

618
00:43:53,297 --> 00:43:55,552
It'll go well. Don't worry.

619
00:43:55,552 --> 00:43:59,327
Hey, and do you know Sae Ryeong's home number?

620
00:44:00,307 --> 00:44:01,934
I don't.

621
00:44:01,934 --> 00:44:04,728
Honestly, these so-called friends...

622
00:44:04,728 --> 00:44:08,148
Should I contact the school?

623
00:44:08,148 --> 00:44:12,112
Her teachers are coming, but
a guardian has to be here.

624
00:44:13,540 --> 00:44:15,009
Sir.

625
00:44:15,848 --> 00:44:17,901
Yes? Go ahead.

626
00:44:18,508 --> 00:44:20,848
What about Sae Ryeong?

627
00:44:20,848 --> 00:44:23,247
Her homeroom teacher would know.

628
00:44:23,247 --> 00:44:24,588
Right?

629
00:44:24,588 --> 00:44:26,123
What about Sae Ryeong?

630
00:44:26,792 --> 00:44:29,165
Why is she such a crazy girl?

631
00:44:53,819 --> 00:44:54,913
Hey.

632
00:44:56,168 --> 00:44:57,398
Drink.

633
00:45:02,035 --> 00:45:04,968
The coach went to Sae Ryeong's house.

634
00:45:04,968 --> 00:45:07,211
It was hard to reach her grandma.

635
00:45:10,901 --> 00:45:12,514
Are you okay?

636
00:45:15,549 --> 00:45:17,068
No.

637
00:45:17,068 --> 00:45:18,501
Not at all.

638
00:45:20,100 --> 00:45:22,263
Why is Sae Ryeong doing this?

639
00:45:25,706 --> 00:45:31,064
[Emergency Medical Center]
Judging by the wounds and scars on her body,

640
00:45:31,064 --> 00:45:34,708
she seems to have self-harmed for years.

641
00:45:35,726 --> 00:45:38,512
She's very emotionally unstable.

642
00:45:38,512 --> 00:45:41,999
A patient like this should never be left alone.

643
00:45:43,202 --> 00:45:45,448
Seriously.

644
00:45:45,448 --> 00:45:48,788
It sounds like she wants me to stay with her.

645
00:45:48,788 --> 00:45:51,095
Just until she calms down. Okay?

646
00:45:51,095 --> 00:45:53,030
- We'll watch her.
- Shin Seung Chan.

647
00:45:55,148 --> 00:45:56,659
What time is it?

648
00:46:01,920 --> 00:46:04,016
[9:30 p.m.]

649
00:46:41,048 --> 00:46:42,304
Sir.

650
00:46:42,304 --> 00:46:43,470
Mom has left.

651
00:46:43,470 --> 00:46:45,472
Yes, I know.

652
00:46:45,472 --> 00:46:48,095
But I can't go home.

653
00:46:48,095 --> 00:46:50,612
Because I'm on call.

654
00:46:51,224 --> 00:46:54,599
I was on call yesterday.
Why am I on call today too?

655
00:46:55,396 --> 00:46:56,897
Kid.

656
00:46:56,897 --> 00:46:59,235
I studied so hard.

657
00:46:59,235 --> 00:47:01,358
Why is my life so exhausting?

658
00:47:03,654 --> 00:47:06,879
Sir, my sister really has nowhere to go.

659
00:47:06,879 --> 00:47:11,495
When I asked, she said she would have to
go back where she used to live.

660
00:47:11,495 --> 00:47:16,997
The good news is the man who hit her
was arrested.

661
00:47:19,253 --> 00:47:21,348
She lives in that gosiwon, right?

662
00:47:21,348 --> 00:47:23,299
Yes, Sir.

663
00:47:23,299 --> 00:47:26,846
Your family is richer than mine,
so why does she live like that?

664
00:47:26,846 --> 00:47:28,347
I know.

665
00:47:30,871 --> 00:47:33,244
So in my house...

666
00:47:34,769 --> 00:47:36,706
there's a living room.

667
00:47:37,900 --> 00:47:39,060
So...

668
00:47:39,860 --> 00:47:43,614
Cho Dul Hee scares me,
but when she's sick, it's a hassle.

669
00:47:43,614 --> 00:47:44,674
Sorry?

670
00:47:44,674 --> 00:47:49,763
So just let her stay at
my place until she's better.

671
00:47:49,763 --> 00:47:52,164
And have her find a new home.

672
00:47:52,164 --> 00:47:55,140
You said she earned so much.
Where did it all go?

673
00:47:55,140 --> 00:47:56,168
Where did it go?

674
00:47:56,168 --> 00:47:57,294
On alcohol.

675
00:47:57,294 --> 00:47:59,937
Her liver must be bad too then.

676
00:48:01,590 --> 00:48:03,054
Thank you, Sir.

677
00:48:03,054 --> 00:48:04,308
As for my mom--

678
00:48:04,308 --> 00:48:06,608
Forget it.

679
00:48:06,608 --> 00:48:08,796
I'm going to go sleep a little now.

680
00:48:08,796 --> 00:48:13,347
Even if I decide to sleep lots,
I only get a little anyway, so a little it is.

681
00:48:14,892 --> 00:48:16,476
Heading down now too?

682
00:48:16,476 --> 00:48:20,272
Yes. My sister's friend is coming,
so I'm heading home.

683
00:48:20,272 --> 00:48:24,780
To cook and do chores and all that. Right?

684
00:48:24,780 --> 00:48:26,541
That's right, Sir.

685
00:48:30,452 --> 00:48:31,816
Kid.

686
00:48:33,121 --> 00:48:34,747
Later,

687
00:48:35,830 --> 00:48:41,823
when I'm not tired, and
your sister isn't scary,

688
00:48:41,823 --> 00:48:46,102
and when you have moved out

689
00:48:46,102 --> 00:48:48,430
and you're doing what you love,

690
00:48:49,399 --> 00:48:51,182
let's meet again then.

691
00:48:53,806 --> 00:48:55,933
Doesn't that mean we'll never meet?

692
00:48:55,933 --> 00:48:57,066
Please.

693
00:48:57,066 --> 00:48:59,355
You're only 20.

694
00:49:00,732 --> 00:49:01,840
Go on.

695
00:49:20,749 --> 00:49:23,085
Honey, are you on your way home?

696
00:49:23,085 --> 00:49:27,864
I got through today somehow,
but I have nothing to say tomorrow.

697
00:49:35,723 --> 00:49:38,004
Excuse me, Manager Kim.

698
00:49:38,004 --> 00:49:42,284
Could you contact my husband for me later?

699
00:49:43,244 --> 00:49:45,110
Tell him I'm on my way now.

700
00:49:45,110 --> 00:49:46,679
Yes, ma'am.

701
00:49:46,679 --> 00:49:48,537
I'll do that.

702
00:49:48,537 --> 00:49:50,025
Thank you.

703
00:51:14,154 --> 00:51:15,909
[I wish you could come soon.
I just want to see your face, even once!]

704
00:51:15,909 --> 00:51:17,881
[But Noh Si Ha, you shouldn't do this to me]

705
00:51:24,847 --> 00:51:26,218
You can go now.

706
00:51:28,130 --> 00:51:30,638
Coach will be here soon.

707
00:51:30,638 --> 00:51:33,058
I'll hand off and leave as soon as he does.

708
00:51:34,325 --> 00:51:35,391
Hey.

709
00:51:35,391 --> 00:51:38,842
You have asked me the time
once a minute since earlier.

710
00:51:38,842 --> 00:51:39,976
You know that?

711
00:51:41,307 --> 00:51:43,055
Meeting someone?

712
00:51:43,729 --> 00:51:45,981
So go.

713
00:51:45,981 --> 00:51:48,201
You're going to see Kim Ha Yeon.

714
00:51:49,379 --> 00:51:50,509
Aren't you?

715
00:51:51,361 --> 00:51:53,924
Yes. Thanks. Really.

716
00:51:53,924 --> 00:51:55,989
- What?
- Thanks a lot.

717
00:52:57,025 --> 00:52:58,374
Ha Yeon!

718
00:53:34,111 --> 00:53:35,512
Yu Gyeom.

719
00:53:42,514 --> 00:53:44,137
Am I very late?

720
00:53:44,137 --> 00:53:45,413
Sorry.

721
00:53:47,769 --> 00:53:49,152
No.

722
00:53:53,109 --> 00:53:54,691
Listen.

723
00:53:57,804 --> 00:54:00,108
I have something to tell you.

724
00:54:06,747 --> 00:54:09,103
Are you breaking up with me?

725
00:54:15,532 --> 00:54:16,877
No.

726
00:54:19,375 --> 00:54:21,950
I'm going to say I was happy.

727
00:54:26,530 --> 00:54:29,340
That it was so fun and good.

728
00:54:34,328 --> 00:54:36,303
I won't forget.

729
00:54:38,403 --> 00:54:41,065
No matter how much time passes.

730
00:54:50,242 --> 00:54:51,834
Listen.

731
00:54:53,092 --> 00:54:55,459
Can I touch you just once?

732
00:55:33,261 --> 00:55:34,675
Yu Gyeom,

733
00:55:35,457 --> 00:55:37,417
I have a dream now.

734
00:55:37,417 --> 00:55:40,180
Really? What is it?

735
00:55:42,926 --> 00:55:44,907
To be happy.

736
00:55:45,634 --> 00:55:47,788
What? That's it?

737
00:55:48,404 --> 00:55:49,817
Yes.

738
00:55:49,817 --> 00:55:52,361
I'll be so happy.

739
00:55:52,361 --> 00:55:54,097
That's my dream.

740
00:55:55,063 --> 00:55:57,442
Then I should be happy too.

741
00:55:58,275 --> 00:56:00,759
What makes you happy?

742
00:56:05,428 --> 00:56:07,084
Think about it.

743
00:56:07,084 --> 00:56:09,244
There must be one thing.

744
00:56:09,244 --> 00:56:11,392
That becomes your dream.

745
00:56:15,954 --> 00:56:18,001
Then for me, the sea...

746
00:56:20,381 --> 00:56:24,663
I want to swim with all my strength
as far as I can go.

747
00:56:25,761 --> 00:56:27,428
That's my dream.

748
00:56:30,274 --> 00:56:32,221
Make that happen.

749
00:56:32,826 --> 00:56:37,272
I like it when you're in the water,
going the farthest.

750
00:56:37,272 --> 00:56:38,562
Ha Yeon.

751
00:56:39,274 --> 00:56:41,786
If I meet you again,

752
00:56:43,589 --> 00:56:46,400
it'll be the moment I watch you do it.

753
00:56:46,400 --> 00:56:48,679
Ha Yeon. Please.

754
00:57:07,714 --> 00:57:09,965
I was eighteen.

755
00:57:09,965 --> 00:57:11,694
It was summer.

756
00:57:11,694 --> 00:57:14,142
Yu Gyeom was in front of me.

757
00:57:14,142 --> 00:57:16,446
It was a rainy night.

758
00:57:22,729 --> 00:57:25,805
I still can't forget that night.

759
00:57:53,553 --> 00:57:58,621
If someone told me to leave just one day
of everything you went through,

760
00:58:01,046 --> 00:58:04,660
It wasn't the night we met
that I wanted to keep.

761
00:58:04,660 --> 00:58:07,986
It was the night we parted.

762
00:58:08,874 --> 00:58:15,246
Some things drain all my feelings
more at the end than at the start.

763
00:58:17,581 --> 00:58:19,478
Love is like that.

764
00:59:02,796 --> 00:59:04,148
You came?

765
00:59:07,759 --> 00:59:09,603
Glad you came, Yu Gyeom.

766
00:59:13,679 --> 00:59:15,003
Yu Gyeom.

767
00:59:15,720 --> 00:59:18,308
You can go anywhere.

768
00:59:18,308 --> 00:59:19,888
I can understand.

769
00:59:19,888 --> 00:59:21,963
Wherever you go, whatever you do.

770
00:59:22,945 --> 00:59:24,304
Really.

771
00:59:24,304 --> 00:59:25,997
I don't care anymore.

772
00:59:27,962 --> 00:59:29,579
But Yu Gyeom,

773
00:59:31,794 --> 00:59:34,108
just come back to me.

774
00:59:37,507 --> 00:59:39,642
Just come back to me like this.

775
00:59:40,410 --> 00:59:42,650
That's all I need.

776
00:59:46,963 --> 00:59:49,448
No rain falls forever.

777
00:59:50,844 --> 00:59:54,465
One day, it will surely clear.

778
01:00:02,936 --> 01:00:06,365
Love is just like that.
